      "id": "old-65-statistical-contract",
      "ref": "3babaa5aa0b11971e20b65625992a9b0dd7b8968",
      "path": "crates/cc-eval/benchmarks/public-v19/protocol/PREREGISTRATION.md",
      "sha256": "dc3f5f89933c6bb403cf65908c9922acd5b817cbb5e6c00c7b2e2d442e36a04c",
      "lines": [
        {
          "line": 35,
          "text": "## Aggregation, paired intervals and margins"
        },
        {
          "line": 36,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 37,
          "text": "Design decision: compute each per-query metric as the arithmetic mean of its3 scheduled repetition scores; repeated requests never multiply N. Report query micro mean over all eligible query variants (transparently counts variants), equal-weight repository macro mean, repository/category cell means and equal-weight category macro mean over nonempty frozen cells. Also report family-balanced means: mean variants within global family, then equal family weight, and within each repo equal-weight family means. Primary quality comparison uses family-balanced repository macro, not a translation-heavy query micro mean. All denominators and missing/unsupported applicability counts accompany each metric; no aggregate includes quarantine. Cross-repo components are single sampling clusters; their repo-specific outcomes stay attached."
        },
        {
          "line": 38,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 39,
          "text": "Freeze paired candidate-minus-baseline per-query deltas, then mean repeated measurements/variants inside a global-family cluster. Primary95% paired family-cluster percentile bootstrap:10000 replicates, seed20261003, deterministic Python `random.Random(seed)` with ordered sorted keys, nearest-rank quantiles ranksceil(.025*B)-1 andceil(.975*B)-1. Design decision, chosen before ranking; not an existing evaluator capability. For components confined to one repo, resample N_repo clusters with replacement independently within each fixed repository, recompute weighted macro/micro using attached cases. For cross-repo components, group by their exact repository-membership signature, resample original N_signature clusters within each signature and carry **all repo outcomes together**; this preserves pairing/leakage units and repository counts without treating a component as independent per repo. Do not split components to obtain narrower intervals. Report fixed six-repository conditional inference, not generalization to all unseen repositories. Category/exact/semantic subgroup use the same cluster draws with pre-frozen eligibility; empty strata produce not_applicable. Fewer than2 independent eligible components or otherwise degenerate/missing denominators =>inconclusive, not bootstrap-certified pass. Two-arm results missing for scheduled cases invalidate comparison; tool failures with valid rows remain observed0 quality and availability failures. Existing cc-eval bootstrap2000 unstratified family means and compare policy are **different diagnostics**, not this global interval."
        },
        {
          "line": 40,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 41,
          "text": "All metrics/deltas and intervals are reported, no post-hoc chosen best metric or slice. Primary native quality nDCG10 and PrimaryTop1 are co-primary descriptive outcomes; compat is separate. Semantic/exact family subsets are pre-frozen via source-task categories/tags and reviewer receipt, never inferred from performance. Any exploratory extra slice is labelled exploratory. No hypothesis selection after ranking. No significance claim that ignores multiple inspected slices; any confirmatory multi-arm extension needs preregistered multiplicity handling before execution."
        },
        {
          "line": 42,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 43,
          "text": "Authority09 §10 suggests absolute nDCG degradation0.01 and PrimaryTop1 one percentage point as **review triggers**, not tolerable correctness errors or automatic acceptance/non-inferiority margins. Freeze those triggers as candidate-minus-baseline mean <-0.01 for each metric; CI crossing a trigger is inconclusive, a reviewer decides next action without changing frozen gold. For performance >10% requires explanation/review, >20% blocks a adequately sampled comparable profile; no latency pass from this quality design (no200-sample tail certification)."
        },
        {
          "line": 44,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 45,
          "text": "**No permissive non-inferiority margin is invented.** Conservative preregistered design choice for a future separately authorized semantic benefit claim: held-out semantic family-balanced nDCG paired95% lower CI>0, and held-out exact family-balanced nDCG and PrimaryTop1 lower CI>=0 (zero tolerated regression in this design), with integrity criteria satisfied. Authority requires semantic gain and no material exact degradation but does not specify this numeric exact bound; zero is explicitly our conservative decision. Current task cannot test these live arms. If unavailable data or CI uncertainty prevents these conditions, status=inconclusive/blocked, never passed. General V19 gate is not automatically decided by these two numerical outcomes: all required corpus, independent review, custody, source/facet/span/availability and reporting obligations remain."
        }
      ]
    },
